{% extends '_base_with_toc.html.twig' %}

{% import '_macros.html.twig' as macros %}

{% block javascripts %}
    {{ parent() }}

    {{ encore_entry_script_tags('creator_card') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}

    {{ encore_entry_link_tags('creator_card') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block title %}labels, verification, reviews{% endblock %}

{% block contents %}
    <h3>State of getfursu.it</h3>

    <p><strong>Changed in 2026</strong>: makers and studios are added without (full) verification, and are labeled as such.</p>

    <h3>What do the labels/markings mean?</h3>

    <p>{{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_PENDING_REVIEW')) }} - this studio/maker has only been <strong>briefly checked</strong>. They may or may not comply with <a href="{{ path('rt_guidelines') }}">the guidelines</a>.</p>

    <p>{{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_ADDED_BEFORE_2026')) }} - added before verification started in 2026. Reviewed only by a single person. May not comply with <a href="{{ path('rt_guidelines') }}">the current guidelines</a>, as they were improved over years.</p>

    <p>{{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_GOT_3_REVIEWS')) }} - added during the 2026 reviews experiment. Checked and accepted by 3 reviewers.</p>

    <p>{{ unverified_item_icon() }} - used to mark maker/studio's offers, products, and styles, which have not yet been verified (studio/maker could not have the skills to produce them; they could not have examples of past works on their websites/social, etc.)</p>

    <p>{{ legacy_verified_item_icon() }} - shown on offers, products, and styles, which were advertised by studios/makers on getfursu.it already, before verification started in 2026.</p>

    <p>{{ verified_item_icon() }} - displayed in front of advertised items, which have been verified.</p>

    <h3>I am an unverified maker; what do I do?</h3>

    <p>While we are figuring out how to approach verifications, feel free to join the efforts; see below.</p>

    <h3>How did we get here?</h3>

    <p>Since the beginning of getfursu.it until 2026 all the requests for being added to the list ("submissions") were being reviewed by a single person; this will no longer be the case. See <a href="https://www.tumblr.com/getfursuit/807379325214162944">this Tumblr post</a> for explanation.</p>

    <p>During 2026, with help from a few volunteers, we've performed a reviews experiment, which resulted in the rejection of a few submissions, addition of 2 studios, and some observations.</p>

    <h3>After the first experiment</h3>

    <p>getfursu.it just got a labels/verifications system. This will allow to add studios/makers early, while marking them as not fully verified. This resolves one significant issue with the reviews experiment: a studio is stuck in the review until last the last remaining issue gets addressed.</p>

    <p>Now, studios will be added after only a basic verification, and marked with the {{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_PENDING_REVIEW')) }} label. This basically means that any information could be inaccurate, or some basic stuff could be even missing.</p>

    <p>Studios added before 2026 will get the {{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_ADDED_BEFORE_2026')) }} label. These studios have been reviewed only by a single person, briefly.</p>

    <p>Studios added during the reviews experiment are marked with {{ macros.label(constant('\\App\\Data\\LabelType::CREATOR_GOT_3_REVIEWS')) }} label. At least three different people reviewed them and agreed on adding.</p>

    <p>Additionally, offers, products, and styles now show the verification status. Until these items will get verified, they will be marked with {{ unverified_item_icon() }}. Items which have been added before the labeling system has been implemented are marked with {{ legacy_verified_item_icon() }}. It should be possible to get them reviewed later.</p>

    <p>Fully verified offers, products, and styles will get the {{ verified_item_icon() }} mark. In the future (near or distant) we may add verification to features, possibly more.</p>

    <h3>What's next</h3>

    <p>We are looking for best ways to verify all the unconfirmed information, and I have no idea how to do that. Share your ideas on the <em>#getfursuit</em> channel on the <a href="https://discord.gg/mep6nUy" target="_blank">FursuitReview's Discord</a>.</p> {# grep-code-fsr-discord-url #}

    <h3>Have questions? AMA</h3>

    <p>Ask through the <a href="{{ path('rt_contact') }}">email or social media</a>. You can also <a href="{{ path('rt_feedback_form') }}">submit anonymous feedback</a> (e.g. "I think you should explain this and that").</p>
{% endblock %}
